**********************************************************************
* metalc_prolog.mac - custom prolog/epilog for Metal C helper        *
* functions (racfree_metal.c, racmode_metal.c) called directly from  *
* hosted-C/LE code (racseq.c) via #pragma linkage(fn, OS).           *
*                                                                    *
* WHY THIS EXISTS (root cause of the U4094-18 abend, 2026-07-29):    *
* Metal C's DEFAULT prolog for any non-"main" function picks up its  *
* own DSA address from the "next save area" (NAB) field at offset+8  *
* of the CALLING function's save area - see z/OS Metal C Programming *
* Guide and Reference, "Compiler-generated default prolog and epilog *
* code": "For functions other than main, the prolog code simply     *
* picks up its DSA pointer (the NAB pointer) from the Address of     *
* next save area field in the calling function's save area."        *
* Hosted C (racseq.c, plain xlc) never populates that field when it  *
* makes an OS-linkage call - it only builds the R1 parameter list.   *
* So the default Metal C prolog ends up loading R13 from garbage,    *
* and every subsequent store relative to R13 writes to a bogus       *
* address ("writing beyond storage" - exactly what abend reason     *
* code X'18' describes). This was confirmed by bisection: even an    *
* empty no-op Metal C function crashed the same way, proving the     *
* fault is in the prolog/epilog mechanics, not in any function body. *
*                                                                    *
* THE FIX (per the same manual, "Supplying your own prolog and       *
* epilog code"): supply custom prolog/epilog that independently      *
* obtains its own DSA via STORAGE OBTAIN/RELEASE - exactly like the  *
* compiler's own default prolog already does for "main" (the one     *
* function that likewise cannot trust an incoming NAB, since it has  *
* no real caller-supplied chain either). MYPROLOG/MYEPILOG below are *
* IBM's own sample macros (SCCNSAM(MYPROLOG)/SCCNSAM(MYEPILOG) in    *
* the z/OS Metal C Programming Guide and Reference), reproduced      *
* verbatim - INCLUDING the "COPY CCNZGBL" line inside each macro,    *
* replaced here with the CCNZGBL GBL declarations inlined directly,  *
* to avoid depending on an external SYSLIB/SCCNSAM search.           *
*                                                                    *
* IMPORTANT (found 2026-07-29, first attempt at this file got it     *
* wrong): the CCN_xxx GBL declarations must NOT be placed once at    *
* file/open-code scope. The Metal C compiler's OWN generated .s      *
* output already declares these same globals in open code (it has   *
* to, in order to SET them before invoking MYPROLOG/MYEPILOG) - a    *
* second open-code GBLA/GBLB/GBLC for the same names is rejected by  *
* HLASM as ASMA004E "Duplicate SET symbol declaration", and worse,   *
* placing our declarations in a separate block meant the compiler's  *
* own MYPROLOG/MYEPILOG invocations (which happen earlier in its own *
* generated code) ran before that block was even reached, producing  *
* ASMA003E "Undeclared variable symbol". IBM's real sample avoids    *
* this entirely by declaring the globals INSIDE each macro body      *
* (matching HLASM's actual scoping rule: a GBLx statement must       *
* appear inside a macro definition for that macro to see the name as *
* global, regardless of any open-code declaration elsewhere) - so    *
* that is what this file does too, exactly like the original.       *
*                                                                    *
* Usage: apply via                                                   *
*   #pragma prolog(function_name, "MYPROLOG")                        *
*   #pragma epilog(function_name, "MYEPILOG")                        *
* on every function in this compilation unit that is called          *
* directly from hosted-C/LE code under OS linkage. This file is      *
* prepended (by build.sh) to the Metal C compiler's generated .s     *
* output before assembly, so these macros are defined before first   *
* use regardless of where in the function list the pragma appears.  *
**********************************************************************
         MACRO
&NAME    MYPROLOG
         GBLA  &CCN_DSASZ    DSA size of the function
         GBLA  &CCN_SASZ     Save area size of this function
         GBLA  &CCN_ARGS     Number of fixed parameters
         GBLA  &CCN_RLOW     1st GPR on STM/STMG in prolog
         GBLA  &CCN_RHIGH    2nd GPR on STM/STMG in prolog
         GBLB  &CCN_MAIN     True if function is main
         GBLB  &CCN_LP64     True if compiled with LP64
         GBLB  &CCN_NAB      True if NAB needed
         GBLB  &CCN_ALTGPR(16) Altered GPRs by the function
         GBLB  &CCN_SASIG    True to gen savearea signature
         GBLC  &CCN_PRCN     Entry symbol of the function
         GBLC  &CCN_CSECT    CSECT name of the file
         GBLC  &CCN_LITN     Symbol name for LTORG
         GBLC  &CCN_BEGIN    Symbol name for function body
         GBLC  &CCN_ARCHLVL  n in ARCH(n) option
         GBLC  &CCN_ASCM     A=AR mode P=Primary mode
         GBLC  &CCN_IASM_MACRO MACRO name for all insert_asm
         GBLB  &CCN_IASM_FRONT True if insert_asm at front
         GBLC  &CCN_NAB_OFFSET Offset to NAB pointer in DSA
         GBLB  &CCN_NAB_STORED True if NAB pointer stored
         GBLC  &CCN_PRCN_LONG Full func name up to 1024 chars
         GBLB  &CCN_STATIC   True if function is static
         GBLB  &CCN_RENT     True if compiled with RENT
         GBLC  &CCN_WSA_INIT WSA initialization function name
         GBLC  &CCN_WSA_TERM WSA termination function name
         GBLB  &CCN_APARSE   True to parse OS PARM
         GBLC  &CCN_DSAUSER  Offset to user field in DSA
         LARL  15,&CCN_LITN
         USING &CCN_LITN,15
         GBLA  &MY_DSASZ
&MY_DSASZ SETA 0
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_1
         STM   14,12,12(13)
         AGO   .NEXT_1
.LP64_1  ANOP
         STMG  14,12,8(13)
.NEXT_1  ANOP
         AIF   (NOT &CCN_RENT).SKIP_R1
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_11
         LR    2,0
         AGO   .SKIP_R1
.LP64_11 ANOP
         LGR   2,0
.SKIP_R1 ANOP
         AIF   (&CCN_DSASZ LE 0).DROP
&MY_DSASZ SETA &CCN_DSASZ
         AIF   (&CCN_DSASZ GT 32767).USELIT
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_2
         LHI   0,&CCN_DSASZ
         AGO   .NEXT_2
.LP64_2  ANOP
         LGHI  0,&CCN_DSASZ
         AGO   .NEXT_2
.USELIT  ANOP
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_3
         L     0,=F'&CCN_DSASZ'
         AGO   .NEXT_2
.LP64_3  ANOP
         LGF   0,=F'&CCN_DSASZ'
.NEXT_2  AIF   (NOT &CCN_NAB).GETDSA
&MY_DSASZ SETA &MY_DSASZ+1048576
         LA    1,1
         SLL   1,20
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_4
         AR    0,1
         AGO   .GETDSA
.LP64_4  ANOP
         AGR   0,1
.GETDSA  ANOP
         STORAGE OBTAIN,LENGTH=(0),BNDRY=PAGE
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_5
         LR    15,1
         ST    15,8(,13)
         L     1,24(,13)
         ST    13,4(,15)
         LR    13,15
         AGO   .CHECK_R
.LP64_5  ANOP
         LGR   15,1
         STG   15,136(,13)
         LG    1,32(,13)
         STG   13,128(,15)
         LGR   13,15
.CHECK_R ANOP
         AIF   (NOT &CCN_RENT).DROP
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_12
         LR    0,2
         AGO   .DROP
.LP64_12 ANOP
         LGR   0,2
.DROP    ANOP
         DROP  15
         MEND
*
         MACRO
&NAME    MYEPILOG
         GBLA  &CCN_DSASZ    DSA size of the function
         GBLA  &CCN_SASZ     Save area size of this function
         GBLA  &CCN_ARGS     Number of fixed parameters
         GBLA  &CCN_RLOW     1st GPR on STM/STMG in prolog
         GBLA  &CCN_RHIGH    2nd GPR on STM/STMG in prolog
         GBLB  &CCN_MAIN     True if function is main
         GBLB  &CCN_LP64     True if compiled with LP64
         GBLB  &CCN_NAB      True if NAB needed
         GBLB  &CCN_ALTGPR(16) Altered GPRs by the function
         GBLB  &CCN_SASIG    True to gen savearea signature
         GBLC  &CCN_PRCN     Entry symbol of the function
         GBLC  &CCN_CSECT    CSECT name of the file
         GBLC  &CCN_LITN     Symbol name for LTORG
         GBLC  &CCN_BEGIN    Symbol name for function body
         GBLC  &CCN_ARCHLVL  n in ARCH(n) option
         GBLC  &CCN_ASCM     A=AR mode P=Primary mode
         GBLC  &CCN_IASM_MACRO MACRO name for all insert_asm
         GBLB  &CCN_IASM_FRONT True if insert_asm at front
         GBLC  &CCN_NAB_OFFSET Offset to NAB pointer in DSA
         GBLB  &CCN_NAB_STORED True if NAB pointer stored
         GBLC  &CCN_PRCN_LONG Full func name up to 1024 chars
         GBLB  &CCN_STATIC   True if function is static
         GBLB  &CCN_RENT     True if compiled with RENT
         GBLC  &CCN_WSA_INIT WSA initialization function name
         GBLC  &CCN_WSA_TERM WSA termination function name
         GBLB  &CCN_APARSE   True to parse OS PARM
         GBLC  &CCN_DSAUSER  Offset to user field in DSA
         GBLA  &MY_DSASZ
         AIF   (&MY_DSASZ EQ 0).NODSA
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_1
         LR    1,13
         AGO   .NEXT_1
.LP64_1  ANOP
         LGR   1,13
.NEXT_1  ANOP
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_2
         L     13,4(,13)
         AGO   .NEXT_2
.LP64_2  ANOP
         LG    13,128(,13)
.NEXT_2  ANOP
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_3
         ST    15,16(,13)
         AGO   .NEXT_3
.LP64_3  ANOP
         STG   15,16(,13)
.NEXT_3  ANOP
         LARL  15,&CCN_LITN
         USING &CCN_LITN,15
         STORAGE RELEASE,LENGTH=&MY_DSASZ,ADDR=(1)
         DROP  15
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_4
         L     15,16(,13)
         AGO   .NEXT_4
.LP64_4  ANOP
         LG    15,16(,13)
.NEXT_4  ANOP
.NODSA   ANOP
         AIF   (&CCN_LP64).LP64_5
         L     14,12(,13)
         LM    1,12,24(13)
         AGO   .NEXT_5
.LP64_5  ANOP
         LG    14,8(,13)
         LMG   1,12,32(13)
.NEXT_5  ANOP
         BR    14
         MEND
